# Block Drop — deploy

- Workflow: `.github/workflows/deploy-block-drop.yml` publishes from `main` when `block-drop/**` changes (or manual dispatch).
- Auth: GitHub OIDC → IAM deploy role. No long-lived AWS access keys in GitHub secrets.
- Repo variables (currently aimed at **prod**): `AWS_DEPLOY_ROLE_ARN`, `AWS_REGION`, `AWS_SITE_BUCKET`, `AWS_DISTRIBUTION_ID`.
- Sync `block-drop/` to the site bucket (exclude README / `.DS_Store`), short `Cache-Control`, then CloudFront `/*` invalidation.
- After renaming deploy role or buckets in Terraform, update those GitHub variables before the next deploy.
- Do not point the deploy role at CloudFormation stack outputs; use Terraform outputs / variables only.
